>I'm not ready to do the Quest yet, the elf tells me. I'm at 81 HP. At
>what level do I get more than one hit a round? 

Why would you genocide mumakil? There are MUCH worse creatures in the
dungeon (about the same level of the mumak is the rust monster, for
example: for a low-level character, this is usually my first pick if I
get to genocide something). You should be able to outrun a mumak,
especially since you are playing an elf (you must be, or your Quest
leader wouldn't be an elf).

You must be level 14 to be allowed to go on the Quest. Since you are
playing an elf, you started out with intrinsic speed, so you already
have more than one hit per round. Maybe you thought the current number
of hits you have was normal: it is not. You are already fast. To get
*very fast*, you should get speed boots or, for temporary effect, zap
yourself with a wand of speed monster or quaff a potion of speed.

But really, my main advice would be to ftp to ftp.krl.caltech.edu, and
get the file beginner.tip (and any other file that you might like over
there).

